 "title": "The Plaster Bodies",
 "sentences": [
  "The bodies of Pompeii aren't bodies: they're hollows in the ash, filled with plaster.",
  "Victims were buried in fine volcanic ash that hardened around them.",
  "Over time their bodies decayed, leaving empty spaces shaped like people.",
  "In 1863, archaeologist Giuseppe Fiorelli poured liquid plaster into those spaces.",
  "When it set, the dead reappeared in their final poses.",
  "Just over a hundred casts have been made this way, and many hold bones inside.",
  "Follow for more from Pompeii."
